From e06620ea01046f3ae9df7eaacaf043dd549dfe9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentine Burley <valentine.burley@collabora.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:24:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tu: Fix software multiview with indirect draws

Restore the SW multiview handling that was dropped in 69f1f21f025.

The original change assumed that this would avoid calling
tu6_emit_vs_params() twice. However, the call in tu_CmdDrawIndirect() is
gated by need_ubo, which is always false on a6xx_gen1_low and a702.

Fixes: 69f1f21f025 ("tu: upload draw_id_offset through driver_params UBO")
Signed-off-by: Valentine Burley <valentine.burley@collabora.com>
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45601>
(cherry picked from commit c8c572b018fd3eee8ff63bc2353d226522498f05)
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index ccff3ea46c1..43deb8ea876 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -9202,6 +9202,16 @@ template <chip CHIP>
 static void
 tu6_emit_empty_vs_params(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd)
 {
+   if (cmd->state.sw_multiview && vs_params_offset(cmd)) {
+      /* We still have to upload the view index of the current replay. Skip the
+       * VFD registers though: CP_DRAW_INDIRECT_MULTI sources VFD_INDEX_OFFSET
+       * and VFD_INSTANCE_START_OFFSET from the indirect buffer, and a draw
+       * state writing them would clobber those values.
+       */
+      tu6_emit_vs_params(cmd, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, /* indirect = */ true);
+      return;
+   }
+
    if (cmd->state.last_vs_params.empty)
       return;
 

From af653c14cef911a11c80988f9d4d013e9f299d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:55:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] freedreno: keep the real subgroup size for OpenCL kernels

OpenCL's subgroup_functions_ballot fails on A702 since compute shaders
with double threadsize bake the subgroup size as a constant: a long16
sub_group_non_uniform_broadcast reads the wrong lane.

api_wavesize = IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY makes get_sub_group_size() a constant 32
there, while real_wavesize stays IR3_SINGLE_OR_DOUBLE and the compiler
still picks a single 16-wide wave for many kernels. GL tolerates a
subgroup with inactive invocations, but CL requires the size to be the
number of work-items actually in it, and rusticl already reports 16 from
the compiled variant.

Leave CL kernels on the driver param, which holds the real wave size.

Fixes: 97abe5b847b5 ("ir3,freedreno: set api_wavesize=IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY for gen6+ compute shaders")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45601>
(cherry picked from commit 10dbbba1df3ca3ae735c254f58681b1f3711741b)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_gallium.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_gallium.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_gallium.c
index 6068fdd1fc3..700b364f101 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_gallium.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_gallium.c
@@ -273,10 +273,12 @@ ir3_shader_compute_state_create(struct pipe_context *pctx,
       if (!ctx->screen->info->props.supports_double_threadsize) {
          api_wavesize = IR3_SINGLE_ONLY;
          real_wavesize = IR3_SINGLE_ONLY;
-      } else {
+      } else if (cso->ir_type != PIPE_SHADER_IR_NIR ||
+                 ((nir_shader *)cso->prog)->info.stage != MESA_SHADER_KERNEL) {
          /* GL has no ALLOW_VARYING_SUBGROUP_SIZE_BIT. Match Turnip's fixed-
           * subgroup-size path: set api_wavesize to IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY so
           * nir_lower_subgroups bakes GL_SUBGROUP_SIZE_KHR as a constant.
+          * CL's get_sub_group_size() must be the real wave size instead.
           */
          api_wavesize = IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY;
       }
